Backport of vLLM PR #54373 (commit d61b6e187, "Take the DFlash draft's RoPE layout from
its own config", Aug 31 2026).

The DFlash loader read is_neox_style off the target's first rotary module and stamped it
onto the draft config. The rotation applies to the draft's own Q/K, so the layout that
has to hold is the one the head was distilled under, not the target's: upstream's case
is GLM-5.3, whose drafter needs neox on an interleaved target (acceptance 1.03 against
7.78 forced to neox), and GLM-5.3-Flash, whose attention has no rope at all so the walk
found the sparse indexer's. The patch removes the inference; a checkpoint distilled
interleaved states it in its own config, everything else keeps the neox default.

No behaviour change for Qwen3.8-27B with its DFlash2 drafter: the target's
Qwen3NextAttention builds its rotary embedding with the default (neox) layout and the
drafter's config does not set is_neox_style, so both paths resolve to the same value.

